  "advisoryReview": {
    "reviewer": "GPT-6 Astra",
    "result": "PASS_NON_AUTHORIZING for a bounded dossier; HOLD translation/admission expansion",
    "snapshot": {
      "head": "a5e3e089ad7a7d3b883dadbfdc660f592b041e24",
      "tree": "a2a94546a8f7556a648bcebf9417c1189f442c05"
    },
    "findings": [
      "wasmHash uses Node SHA-256; Ed25519 signs a domain-separated UTF-8 preimage containing hash and profile. Preserve separators, encoding, base64 and crypto error behavior; certified policy forces signature verification, while a matching-hash unsigned attestation can pass when signed/certified requirements are absent.",
      "admitAndInstantiate verifies before linking and wraps instantiation failures, but WebAssembly start functions may execute before memory binding and observer callbacks can replace the intended error. Admission does not establish bounded execution or immutable artifact ownership.",
      "HostRuntime contains mutable registries, WebAssembly memory and console/output effects. The closed-import claim depends on the caller supplying a trusted HostRuntime; observer callbacks are behaviorally observable.",
      "Marshalling mixes code-point length/character indexing with UTF-16 slicing/search/comparison, uses opaque handles and sentinels, and mutates registries. Record staging uses heap base 1024, four-byte slots and a monotonic bump with scoped collision assumptions.",
      "Seam adapters parse and bind hashes and require a named function export, but low-level execution performs no attestation check and accepts finite numeric values whose WASM ABI coercion remains observable. Generic strings/records, timeouts and per-export authorization are absent.",
      "The three Fungi assets return only the admission-domain string and ABI constants; they provide no crypto, host runtime, marshalling or admission replacement."
    ],
    "materialObligations": [
      "Preserve hash/signature domain encoding, profile binding, base64 and fail-closed crypto errors.",
      "Preserve attestation-before-linking order, start-function behavior, observer ordering and supplied-host custody.",
      "Preserve handle aliasing, mutable registries, UTF-16/code-point distinctions, sentinels, i32 coercion and record bump/capacity behavior.",
      "Keep the low-level executor composition-gated; preserve named function-export checks, numeric ABI limits, trap/link classification and no timeout guarantee.",
      "Treat existing Fungi constants as non-authorizing and retain TypeScript as the consumer shadow."
    ]
  },
